Article 27
(1) Efforts to prevent violence against Women and Children are carried out in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. PPPA;
b. social;
c. health;
d. education;
e. manpower;
f. population and civil registration;
g. law;
h. cooperatives and micro enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual; and
j. peace and order.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by means of:
a. building cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, as well as Educational Institutions, Health, hospitals, various NGOs that care about women and children;
b. building community and family participation and concern towards the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
c. establishing a violence prevention system that provides a complete and easily accessible information system;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. providing critical education about the rights of women and children as victims of violence to the community; and
f. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), is implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

Article 40
Special Protection for children in Conflict with (1) the Law as referred to in Article 38 Paragraph (2) letter b, shall be carried out through:
a. humane treatment with attention to needs according to their age, separation from adults;
b. provision of legal assistance and other assistance effectively;
c. implementation of recreational activities;
d. freedom from torture, punishment, or other treatment that is cruel, inhumane, and degrading to dignity and degree;
e. avoidance of imposition of the death penalty and/or life imprisonment;
f. avoidance of arrest, detention, or imprisonment, except as a last resort and for the shortest period of time;
g. provision of justice before a juvenile court that is objective, impartial, and in a hearing closed to the public;
h. avoidance of publication of their identity;
i. provision of accompaniment by parents/guardians and persons trusted by the child;
j. provision of social advocacy;
k. provision of private life;
l. provision of accessibility, especially for children with disabilities;
m. provision of Education;
n. provision of health services; and
o. provision of other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) Special Protection for Children in Conflict with the Law as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through efforts of:
a. prevention,
b. administrative settlement of cases;
c. rehabilitation; and
d. social reintegration.

