Article 21
The Regional Government conducts empowerment and (1) awareness raising to families, parents, and the community. The empowerment and awareness raising as referred to (2) in paragraph (1) shall be conducted by means of:
a. providing materials on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. creating a friendly and safe work environment atmosphere for women;
d. building community participation and concern towards the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing an information system that is easily accessible;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and g. providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.

